+## Direct SCRAM and database credential clock fixture
+
+This private source candidate preserves the accepted creator-edge policy and
+existing socket-trust fixture. A separate trusted package-input format binds
+the experimental direct SCRAM profile. For that profile `_auth` checks the
+actual session authentication method and TCP peer, then requires a finite role
+`VALID UNTIL` ahead of the current database wall clock. The existing deferred
+COMMIT path invokes the same guard. Historical readback remains scoped to the
+actual live reader and retains historical writer associations.
+
+The isolated fixture uses the tracked test CA and SCRAM verifier generator.
+Actors connect only over the owned container loopback with `verify-full` and
+required channel binding. The new case stages a recorder Acquire before its
+real finite deadline, observes independent original absence, and sends
+literal COMMIT after the deadline while the requested 60-second fence would
+still be fresh. The intended refusal preserves all committed snapshots and
+exact independent Install readback. A separate fresh recorder login must
+fail. This slice has one shared login and operation deadline per actor. It
+adds no managed activation, write/recovery handoff or retirement authority.
